================================================================================
TEST 47210 -- MAC/Phy TLV with combination of user defined speed, duplex and auto nego
================================================================================
Run:      2026-10-09 19:02:59-19:10:28 NZDT (tb470 time; the x230 holds NZ wall time labelled
          UTC, ~2 s behind tb470; the AR4050S clock is NZDT)
Bench:    tb470, consoles u0 (x230, DUT), u1 (AR4050S); Test Engineer terrenceb@terrenceb-dl
Tester:   bench-runner (by hand: tools/tb ckcon -> tools/ckcon.py with its @poll directive,
          tools/rcdiff.py, tools/rc2cfg.py; no framework script)
Graded:   tester
Case:     AWPTCM-T47210 (Draft), objective and precondition empty, 1 step (step text and
          expected result empty)
Build:    swi_f awplus_main-20261008-57 (x230v2_28GS-awplus_main-20261008-57.rel), bootloader 6.2.40
          swi_e awplus_main-20261008-57 (AR4050S-5G)
Configs:  swi_f.cfg, swi_e.cfg (running-config with the case setup applied; in swi_e.cfg
          port1.0.2 reads shutdown, while during the case it was `no shutdown` (STEP 0);
          saved to startup: no)

VERDICT: PASS -- for 9 user-defined speed/duplex/autonegotiation combinations on x230 port1.0.1,
         the x230's IEEE 802.3 MAC/PHY Configuration/Status TLV, decoded by the AR4050S, showed
         the matching autonegotiation state, advertised set and operational MAU type
      combination (x230 / AR4050S)        autoneg              advertised                      MAU
      C1 auto / auto ................ PASS  Supported, Enabled   1000TFD,100TXFD,100TX,10TFD,10T  1000BaseTFD (30)
      C2 auto 100 / auto ............ PASS  Supported, Enabled   100BaseTXFD, 100BaseTX           100BaseTXFD (16)
      C3 auto 100 half / auto ....... PASS  Supported, Enabled   100BaseTX                        100BaseTXHD (15)
      C9 auto 10 / auto ............. PASS  Supported, Enabled   10BaseTFD, 10BaseT               10BaseTFD (11)
      C8 1000 full fixed / auto ..... PASS  Supported, Disabled  [none]                           1000BaseTFD (30)
      C4 100 full / 100 full ........ PASS  Supported, Disabled  [none]                           100BaseTXFD (16)
      C5 100 half / 100 half ........ PASS  Supported, Disabled  [none]                           100BaseTXHD (15)
      C6 10 full / 10 full .......... PASS  Supported, Disabled  [none]                           10BaseTFD (11)
      C7 10 half / 10 half .......... PASS  Supported, Disabled  [none]                           10BaseTHD (10)
CAVEAT:  one link only: x230 port1.0.1 (AT-SPTXa copper SFP) against the AR4050S's fixed copper
         port1.0.2, the only x230 link on this bench whose partner runs 10 Mb/s and half duplex.
         With a fixed `speed 1000` (C8) the x230 reports autoneg "Supported, Disabled" and
         advertised [none] while the partner reads a-full a-1000; the TLV reflects the configured
         mode. Whether that is the intended report for 1000BASE-T is for the case owner.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TOPOLOGY AS TESTED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  DUT     : swi_f (AT-x230-28GS V2, hostname awplus) console u0, S/N A10783G262900002,
            system MAC 00c2.8f3f.0f5d, boot config flash:/default.cfg
  partner : swi_e (AR4050S-5G, hostname 4050-5g) console u1, S/N A10401G214000005,
            LLDP chassis 0000.cd40.0394, management address 10.10.10.2,
            boot config flash:/tb470-bench.cfg
  link    : swi_f port1.0.1 (AT-SPTXa A04906R191400072, 1000BASE-T) <-> swi_e port1.0.2
            (fixed copper, 10/100/1000, half and full), x230 VLAN 101 (alone, this case) /
            AR4050S VLAN 10; `lldp tlv-select mac-phy-config` on both ends (this case)
  other   : the x230's other links (port1.0.2-1.0.5 to the IE520 stack and tb470 eth3) were
            untouched
  bench   : spanning tree disabled on the x230 and the AR4050S; x230 `lldp run`
  tools   : on tb470: tools/tb ckcon tb470 x230port-1840 <uN> 115200 [--stop-on-error] <commands>
            (tools/ckcon.py). `@poll <s> <regex> <cmd>` re-runs <cmd> until the output matches
            (here: the expected TLV fields at the AR4050S) and prints the time taken.
            "HH:MM:SS >>> <cmd>" below is the tb470 time the command was sent. In each LLDP
            detail only the identity and the MAC/PHY lines are quoted; every other TLV read
            "[not advertised]"

